# VetGigaGraph — Environment Variables Template
#
# How to use:
#   1. Copy this file to .env (which is gitignored):
#      $ cp .env.example .env
#   2. Fill in real values in .env (NEVER commit .env)
#   3. Tokens are loaded automatically by src/utils/env.py at startup
#
# All values are optional unless marked [REQUIRED].
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. Blank lines are ignored.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hugging Face Hub — required for GigaPath model access
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GigaPath (prov-gigapath/prov-gigapath) is a GATED model on Hugging Face.
#
# Steps:
#   1. Create an account at https://huggingface.co/ and verify your email.
#   2. Visit https://huggingface.co/prov-gigapath/prov-gigapath and click
#      "Agree and access repository" (one-time gated-model gate).
#   3. Generate a User Access Token at https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
#      with the `read` role (the `read` role is sufficient for this project).
#   4. Paste the token below as HF_TOKEN.
#
# The token is consumed by:
#   - src/utils/env.py::load_env() at import time
#   - timm.create_model("hf_hub:prov-gigapath/prov-gigapath", pretrained=True)
#   - huggingface_hub library (auto-detects HF_TOKEN env var)
#
# [REQUIRED for Phase 3+]
HF_TOKEN=hf_replace_this_with_your_actual_token

# Optional: separate cache directory for HF downloads. Default is
# ~/.cache/huggingface. Setting HF_HOME redirects all HF cache to one place.
# Recommended: keep HF cache off the repo and off /tmp (4GB+ for GigaPath).
# HF_HOME=/data/cia_outputs/.hf_cache

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weights & Biases — optional, used for experiment logging
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generate at https://wandb.ai/authorize. If unset, training runs proceed
# with a no-op logger (see src/utils/logger.py::wandb_run).
#
# WANDB_API_KEY=your_wandb_api_key_here
# WANDB_PROJECT=vetgigagraph
# WANDB_ENTITY=your_username_or_team
# WANDB_MODE=online            # online | offline | disabled

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compute / runtime knobs (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
# OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
# TORCH_COMPILE_DEBUG=1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data locations (optional — the defaults are shown)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by the configs (configs/*.yaml, via ${oc.env:...}), by the scripts
# (src/utils/env.py: raw_dir(), output_dir(), ...) and by the shell scripts.
# Paths recorded in results/*.json are written relative to these variables,
# e.g. "$VETGIGA_OUTPUT_DIR/checkpoints/...".
#
# CATCH whole-slide images: <dir>/<class>/<class>_<id>_<slot>.svs
# VETGIGA_RAW_DIR=/data/cancerImagingArchive
# Derived data: tiles, features, graphs, splits, checkpoints, logs
# VETGIGA_OUTPUT_DIR=/data/cia_outputs
# Run directory of the original GigaPath-DefGNN training (fold_<i>/checkpoints/);
# default: ../vetgigagraph_v2/results/deformable next to this repository
# DEFGNN_RUN_DIR=
# Checkout of the v1 static-graph repository (scripts/01_capture_v1_reference.py);
# default: ../pw-vetGigagraph next to this repository
# V1_ROOT=
